window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Seven days to make her remember. Seven nights to make her beg.</b></p> <p>She was my salvation—until she became my destruction.<br> <b>Once, I would have bled for her.</b><br> Now, I burn for revenge.<br> She and her father didn’t just betray me. They <b>destroyed</b> me. Left me broken, bleeding, crawling my way out of hell. And now, years later, she’s back—wrapped up in a satin bow with a <b>convenient case of amnesia</b>?<br> Nice try, princess. But I don’t believe in fairy tales.<br> I bought her at an auction. <b>Now I own her for a week.</b><br> Seven days to make her remember exactly who she was to me.<br> Seven nights to make her pay for every lie.<br> And when I’ve broken her, when I’ve ruined her the way she ruined me…<br> She’ll beg me to keep her.<br> And I will.<br> Because after seven days, I won’t be able to let her go.<br> Not now. Not ever.</p> <p><b>Just seven days to make her mine. Forever.</b></p> <p><i>Note: formerly called Cherry Auction</i></p> <p><i>TWs: Please note this is a dark romance with kidnapping, dub-con, and intense themes of mental illness, abuse and trauma (including references to past childhood abuse). A full list of trigger warnings can be found on the author’s website.</i></p>"; 
